 **Decision:** The owner requested a person driving a wagon or carriage around a loop in1835 and1904 with walk-up interaction. The1835 demonstration uses a reconstructed18m-radius circle on level ground southwest of town, with no historical-road, hotel-proximity or recorded-journey claim. The unchanged1904 carriageway candidate remains physically unqualified on the actual street ground. The exact vehicles, horses, team assignment, timetable and route are reconstructed activity. Otis's existing1835 figure is temporarily transferred rather than duplicated; Hans Johnson's existing inferred1904 coachman identity retains its census1900 basis and uncertain continued presence, while appearance, seated action and this journey remain reconstructed. No household carriage ownership, attested trip, archival likeness or dialogue is manufactured. Stop/continue is the first interaction; boarding, riding, force physics, broader photographic quality and continuous world contact remain separate acceptance questions.
 
+**Seated looking supplement, 2026-11-03:** The original eight-second `sit_drive_look_v2` action adds neck yaw up to 3 degrees, head yaw up to 4 degrees and head nod up to 1.5 degrees to the actual exported seated poses of Otis and Hans. These amplitudes and timing are reconstructed authoring choices, not an observed habit, documented event or archival likeness. Only two rotation curves change; the original seated/walk/standing clips, torso, arms, palms, pelvis, legs, geometry, skinning and graphical source notices remain. Active master/web LOD0 and LOD3 exports carry the same action. The driver uses a separate visual clock while the vehicle is stopped; animation holds, Reduced Motion, hidden figures/tabs, draw reach and Light continue to suspend it. Finite native loader/mixer readback at 65 keys and 64 midpoints finds unchanged protected body transforms/Float32 skin palettes and identical selected Hans palm points; it does not establish continuous garment fit, full occupied-world contact, photographic quality, boarding or riding. The derivative, actual native readback and original-parent palm binding bridge are recorded under `data/humans/animations/seated-driver-look-v2.*.json`.
+
 **Recorded:** 2026-11-02.
 
